    ## Manual Verification Steps for Iteration 1 Backend

    Here's what you can verify right now:

    ### 1. Login with Default Owner
    ```bash
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "admin", "password": "admin"}' \
      -c /tmp/cookies.txt -i
    ```
    ✓ Should return 200 OK with `{"message":"Login successful","username":"admin","role":"owner"}`
    ✓ Should set HttpOnly cookie

    ### 2. Get Current User
    ```bash
    curl -X GET http://localhost:8081/api/auth/me -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should return owner user details

    ### 3. List Users (as owner)
    ```bash
    curl -X GET http://localhost:8081/api/users -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should return list with 1 user (admin)

    ### 4. Create Admin User
    ```bash
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/users \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "admin_user", "password": "admin123", "role": "admin"}' \
      -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should create new admin user

    ### 5. Create Viewer User
    ```bash
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/users \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "viewer_user", "password": "viewer123", "role": "viewer"}' \
      -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should create new viewer user

    ### 6. Change Owner Password
    ```bash
    curl -X PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/users/1 \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"password": "newpassword"}' \
      -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should update password successfully

    ### 7. Login as Admin
    ```bash
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "admin_user", "password": "admin123"}' \
      -c /tmp/admin_cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Verify admin can login and manage users

    ### 8. Login as Viewer (Test Read-Only)
    ```bash
    # Login as viewer
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "viewer_user", "password": "viewer123"}' \
      -c /tmp/viewer_cookies.txt

    # Try to create user (should fail)
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/users \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{"username": "test", "password": "test123", "role": "viewer"}' \
      -b /tmp/viewer_cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should return 403 Forbidden

    ### 9. Try to Delete Self (Should Fail)
    ```bash
    curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/users/1 -b /tmp/cookies.txt -i
    ```
    ✓ Should return 400 with "You cannot delete your own account"

    ### 10. Try to Delete Owner (Should Fail)
    ```bash
    # As admin, try to delete owner
    curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/users/1 -b /tmp/admin_cookies.txt -i
    ```
    ✓ Should return 400 with "Owner accounts cannot be deleted"

    ### 11. Logout
    ```bash
    curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/logout -b /tmp/cookies.txt
    ```
    ✓ Should clear cookie

    ### 12. Database Verification
    ```bash
    docker exec claude-db psql -U ddms -d ddms -c "SELECT id, username, role FROM users;"
    ```
    ✓ Should show all created users with correct roles

    All these tests should pass based on the implementation. The backend is fully functional and ready for frontend integration!
